    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: BRT operations established 
Indicator: One biogas production plant built and operated through a DBO contract, ensuring at least 80% of the required fuel supply for the fleet 
Progress/Status: due to the change in propulsion technology from CNG to full-electric, the biogas produced will now be sold to the market and a percentage of the revenue will be given to TKC as non-fare revenue to subsidize the cost of electricity it purchases from the grid, improving the system&amp;apos;s financial sustainability. Its CAPEX also significantly increased from USD 10.2 million [initial costing] to USD 27 million [revised costing based on the feasibility study and updated items&amp;apos; rate]. The plant will now be conceived as a commercially viable standalone project financed under a PPP arrangement, through (i) a mix of debt and equity from the private concessionaire/operator; and (ii) a viability gap funding [VGF] up to USD 14 million from the GCF [USD 10.2 million concessional loan + USD 3.8 million grant]. The project is being restructured by TKC with the support of ADB-financed consultants. 
Data Source: TransKarachi quarterly project implementation progress reports 
